WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.294 --> 00:00:01.877
Good morning Hank, 
it's Thursday 

00:00:01.961 --> 00:00:05.589
And the greatest ever Pizzamas, 
at least in terms of shirt sales, 

00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:07.173
is about to come to an end.

00:00:07.215 --> 00:00:08.425
That's right Hank,
nothing lasts forever 

00:00:08.466 --> 00:00:11.677
Not even cold November rain and
tomorrow marks the end of 

00:00:11.719 --> 00:00:15.389
week daily videos and soon you will
be unable to get this shirt 

00:00:15.431 --> 00:00:18.711
or any of the other amazing
Pizzamas stuff available at

00:00:18.771 --> 00:00:21.674
Pizzamas.com right now but
only for the next couple days.

00:00:21.874 --> 00:00:24.689
Now listen Hank, I don't want to end 
my part of Pizzamas on a bummer note

00:00:24.731 --> 00:00:27.650
 but I do have to take next 
week off from Vlogbrothers

00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:29.360
Because I'll be traveling with my family 

00:00:29.402 --> 00:00:32.029
Specifically, I'll be traveling to 
England to see my friend 

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:35.228
Mike Birbiglia perform
comedy and my football team

00:00:35.329 --> 00:00:37.325
AFC Wimbledon perform tragedy

00:00:37.367 --> 00:00:39.452
Or at least that's what the
betting odds would indicate

00:00:39.494 --> 00:00:40.578
But you never know with Wimbledon 

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:43.330
America's second  favorite 
fourth tier English soccer team,

00:00:43.372 --> 00:00:45.999
that most people
in this community keep up with

00:00:46.059 --> 00:00:49.802
via updates on Dear Hank and
John, our hit podcast that

00:00:49.863 --> 00:00:52.385
unfortunately has been on
cancer hiatus for the last

00:00:52.405 --> 00:00:55.368
several months, which means
that most of y'all probably

00:00:55.428 --> 00:00:57.635
don't know what's happening
with AFC Wimbledon

00:00:57.676 --> 00:01:00.304
Single sentence backstory for anyone
who's new, my producing partner

00:01:00.345 --> 00:01:03.348
Rosianna and I sponsor
a fourth tier English soccer team 

00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:05.767
called AFC Wimbledon who
play in South London

00:01:05.808 --> 00:01:10.580
And who are owned by their fans 
each of whom pay about $25 a year

00:01:10.580 --> 00:01:13.065
In order to vote on the club's leadership

00:01:13.107 --> 00:01:15.525
Because of that sponsorship, 
Wimbledon's women's team play 

00:01:15.567 --> 00:01:17.861
with a Partners in Health logo 
on the back of their shirts

00:01:17.902 --> 00:01:22.114
and the men's team play with a DFTBA
logo on the back of their shorts 

00:01:22.156 --> 00:01:24.742
in that liminal space
between left thigh and buttock

00:01:24.783 --> 00:01:26.410
The other thing you need to 
know about AFC Wimbledon 

00:01:26.452 --> 00:01:28.188
is that we're bad

00:01:28.203 --> 00:01:30.705
Like, there are other teams in 
the fourth tier of English football 

00:01:30.747 --> 00:01:35.168
who are owned by major Hollywood 
celebrities, or the Saudi government, 

00:01:35.209 --> 00:01:38.462
but we are owned by our fans and
so we never have any money

00:01:38.504 --> 00:01:41.173
So we've got a beautiful new
stadium owned and built by the fans 

00:01:41.215 --> 00:01:42.715
that's packed every week

00:01:42.715 --> 00:01:43.633
What we don't have is

00:01:43.675 --> 00:01:45.093
uh... money

00:01:45.135 --> 00:01:46.094
So we're pretty bad every year

00:01:46.136 --> 00:01:47.804
We used to be a third tier 
English soccer team

00:01:47.845 --> 00:01:51.033
 but then we got relegated down to 
the fourth tier because we were so bad

00:01:51.053 --> 00:01:55.060
and then we barely survived in
the fourth tier last season

00:01:55.102 --> 00:01:57.270
and this season wasn't looking
like it was going to be any different 

00:01:57.312 --> 00:01:59.091
except something
weird happened which is that

00:01:59.091 --> 00:01:59.811
uh... 

00:01:59.811 --> 00:02:01.357
we seem like we might be good? 

00:02:01.399 --> 00:02:03.776
Like, not to brag, but if you 
look at the table currently 

00:02:03.818 --> 00:02:05.820
AFC Wimbledon are narrowly 
ahead of Wrexham

00:02:05.861 --> 00:02:09.153
the football club owned by 
Ryan Reynolds and Rob McElhaney

00:02:09.153 --> 00:02:10.619
and we're several spots above

00:02:10.659 --> 00:02:13.121
the franchise currently plying
its trade in Milton Keynes

00:02:13.285 --> 00:02:15.245
Also, and this is even more surprising,

00:02:15.297 --> 00:02:17.038
we're fun to watch this season

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:19.540
 We have exciting young players 
who score lots of goals 

00:02:19.582 --> 00:02:21.792
and also a mountain of a man

00:02:21.835 --> 00:02:25.379
who rolls his shorts up so much 
that you can't even see our logo

00:02:25.420 --> 00:02:26.755
but more on him in a second

00:02:26.796 --> 00:02:28.339
So our star players this year include our

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:31.108
striker Ali al-Hamadi 
who left Iraq

00:02:31.134 --> 00:02:34.803
as an infant after his dad was imprisoned 
by the Saddam Hussein regime

00:02:34.845 --> 00:02:36.847
and now has become an 

00:02:36.889 --> 00:02:39.850
Absolute superstar for both 
AFC Wimbledon 

00:02:39.891 --> 00:02:41.775
and the Iraqi national team

00:02:41.810 --> 00:02:43.436
I just love him so much.
Also we have 

00:02:43.519 --> 00:02:45.188
the mustachioed James Tilly

00:02:45.229 --> 00:02:48.399
who scored seven goals 
in his first nine games for us

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:49.441
And out on the other wing we've got

00:02:49.483 --> 00:02:51.568
Aaron Sassu, an 18 year old

00:02:51.610 --> 00:02:54.946
who's been playing for Wimbledon's 
youth side since he was 10

00:02:54.988 --> 00:02:57.323
In fact, there are a bunch of great players 
emerging from our academy

00:02:57.365 --> 00:02:58.157
 Our fullbacks include 

00:02:58.199 --> 00:03:01.869
my personal hero Jack Curry, who's also
played with us since he was 10

00:03:01.911 --> 00:03:04.913
and also Isaac Ovandera,
who joined us at the age of 14

00:03:04.955 --> 00:03:07.327
We're never gonna be
the kind of football club that

00:03:07.367 --> 00:03:10.835
can buy big stars, so we're
gonna have to make them

00:03:10.877 --> 00:03:12.920
 and we've done a 
really good job of that

00:03:12.962 --> 00:03:14.964
And then we have our central defenders

00:03:15.006 --> 00:03:16.841
Ryan Greatbeard Johnson

00:03:16.882 --> 00:03:19.009
and Mighty Joe Lewis

00:03:19.051 --> 00:03:21.762
Joe Lewis, the man
with the golden shorts. 

00:03:21.803 --> 00:03:23.763
Joe "Shortshorts" Lewis

00:03:23.805 --> 00:03:26.077
Joe "big man, small shorts" Lewis

00:03:26.077 --> 00:03:28.851
Joe "we're only here for the shorts" Lewis 

00:03:28.893 --> 00:03:31.649
Look at how aggressively this man 
rolls up his shorts

00:03:31.687 --> 00:03:33.814
You cannot see our DFTBA logo

00:03:33.855 --> 00:03:37.150
and I, for one, am fine with it

00:03:37.192 --> 00:03:38.687
The great thing about AFC Wimbledon is that

00:03:38.687 --> 00:03:42.113
If you love an underdog story
we keep on delivering 

00:03:42.154 --> 00:03:45.241
because we're always going 
to be an underdog story

00:03:45.282 --> 00:03:46.450
But the argument we've been making 

00:03:46.492 --> 00:03:48.702
in the 10 years we've been
sponsoring AFC Wimbledon 

00:03:48.744 --> 00:03:51.996
and the 21 years since AFC
Wimbledon reformed 

00:03:52.038 --> 00:03:54.040
after being told by the English FA that 

00:03:54.082 --> 00:03:57.168
there was no place for a 
football club in that community

00:03:57.209 --> 00:04:01.380
 community-held assets, 
communal action can work

00:04:01.421 --> 00:04:05.050
It's not easy, it doesn't 
always work, but it can work

00:04:05.091 --> 00:04:08.049
I know it's just a football club, but what I've
learned from AFC Wimbledon,

00:04:08.069 --> 00:04:11.630
not just on the field but also
their local action group that

00:04:11.670 --> 00:04:13.682
seeks to address 
poverty in the community 

00:04:13.724 --> 00:04:17.477
and the AFC Wimbledon Foundation
what I've learned from them 

00:04:17.519 --> 00:04:22.093
I've used and we've used in a lot
of our community projects

00:04:22.153 --> 00:04:27.528
including trying to get folks to lower 
the prices of TB diagnostics and treatments

00:04:27.569 --> 00:04:29.655
And I'll tell you what, I'm sure we're 
not gonna be good all season

00:04:29.696 --> 00:04:34.492
I'm sure we're gonna lose a bunch of our best
players in the January transfer window, etc.

00:04:34.534 --> 00:04:36.869
But oh my gosh, is it fun when we're good

00:04:36.953 --> 00:04:38.412
And holy crap, I love Pizzamas

00:04:38.454 --> 00:04:40.789
Thanks for coming up with 
this weird idea, Hank.

00:04:40.831 --> 00:04:44.543
I'm gonna savor saying this since 
I won't get to say it for a year

00:04:44.584 --> 00:04:46.169
I will see you tomorrow

